("L19","So let's run the face-off. Four Canadians, four very different tax years. Same rules for everyone."),
("L20","Round one. Ava. She's twenty-two, a university student, with one part-time job. Her total income for the year is fourteen thousand dollars."),
("L21","And Ava is the easiest case in this whole video, because almost everybody wants to give her a free return."),
("L22","H and R Block is free for anyone twenty-five or younger. Every package. No income limit."),
("L23","UFile is free for post-secondary students, and also free when total family income is under twenty thousand dollars."),
("L24","StudioTax is free when total income is under twenty thousand. Wealthsimple Basic can be zero. CloudTax Basic covers employment income, for zero. And GenuTax is always zero."),
("L25","So Ava's real cost is zero dollars, six different ways. If any app asks her to upgrade, the honest answer is no."),
("L26","One more option for Ava. If her income is modest and her return is simple, a free tax clinic, run by volunteers through a CRA program, can file it for her. And the CRA's own SimpleFile service is free for eligible people with a lower income."),
