("L27","Round two. Liam. One job, one T4, sixty-eight thousand dollars. He gave to a charity, and he has some medical receipts."),
("L28","This is where the free tiers start to split."),
("L29","At TurboTax and H and R Block, donations and medical expenses sit in the Deluxe tier. That's thirty dollars, or twenty-nine ninety-nine."),
("L30","At UFile, the free option is for a single T4 with only the standard credits. Donations and medical expenses take Liam past that. So UFile Online starts at twenty dollars ninety-five."),
("L31","StudioTax is seventeen fifty, because his income is over twenty thousand. Wealthsimple says every form is in every plan, including donations and medical. So Basic can still be zero. Same with GenuTax."),
("L32","Same return, same tax law. A price range from zero to thirty dollars. The difference is the interface, and the help, not the result."),
# ACT 6 ROUND 3
("L33","Round three. Priya. Salary plus a brokerage account. This year she sold shares, so she has capital gains to report, and some foreign dividends."),
("L34","At TurboTax, capital gains and foreign income are in Premier, fifty dollars. At H and R Block, Premier is forty-nine ninety-nine."),
