("L38","Round four. Marc. He's self-employed, he does freelance design, and he rents out a basement suite."),
("L39","Marc's deadlines are different. As a self-employed person, he can file until June fifteenth. But any tax he owes is still due by April thirtieth. Interest starts on the money, not on the paperwork."),
("L40","At TurboTax, self-employment and rental income are in the Self-Employed tier. Seventy dollars. H and R Block, sixty-nine ninety-nine."),
("L41","StudioTax says it covers self-employed returns and rental income. Seventeen fifty. GenuTax lists rental properties and small business, for free."),
("L42","Wealthsimple Basic still claims rental income and every form, at any price, including zero."),
("L43","So on price alone, Marc could pay anywhere from zero to seventy dollars for the same two forms."),
