("L51","Final face-off. The three questions that decide your pick."),
("L52","Question one. How complex is your year? One T4 and the standard credits, almost anything free will do. Investments, rental, or self-employment, check which tier unlocks those forms before you start."),
("L53","Question two. How much help do you want? None, take the free option. Some reassurance, look at audit protection. A real person to review it, that's the expert tiers, and they cost more."),
("L54","Question three. What device, and where do you live? GenuTax is Windows only. StudioTax runs on Windows, Mac, iPhone and Android. And if you file in Quebec, check each program's limits, because Wealthsimple's Pro plan, for example, isn't offered in Quebec."),
# ACT 11 VERDICT
("L55","So here's the verdict. There's no single winner. The right program depends on your tax year, and on how much help you want."),
("L56","Student or low income: file free. H and R Block if you're twenty-five or under, UFile or StudioTax under twenty thousand, or a free tax clinic."),
("L57","Simple T4 with a few credits: a free tier that includes donations and medical, like Wealthsimple Basic or GenuTax, does the same job as a thirty-dollar tier."),
("L58","Investors and self-employed: free options exist, but read the limits. And if you want a safety net, that's what you're paying for."),
